  "limitations": "Exactly one panel: no adaptive subdivision, infinite bounds, singularity detection or QAGS/QAGI implementation. The error estimate is heuristic and may underestimate aliased/narrow features. sin/cos/exp use radians/dimensionless x. bessel_integrand is cos(order*x-argument*sin(x))/pi; it only represents the conventional Bessel integral on [0,pi]. Overflow is an error. Zero-width intervals return zero without sampling.",
  "port_notes": "Faithful double-precision DQK21 abscissae and weights, even/odd node evaluation order, Gauss comparison, absolute integral, mean-deviation integral, resasc-based error rescaling and 50*machine-epsilon roundoff floor. The upstream prologue dates the Fortran routine to 1980 with a 1983 revision. Only a safe finite set of integrands replaces Fortran callbacks; this does not port the full adaptive QUADPACK driver. Original Fortran was not compiled in this environment.",
